# V83 — visible child calf study, not adopted

Source V75. Original curve remains hidden, unmodified. New evaluated mesh has Basis and a reversible localized posterior-calf shape key; setting it to zero restores evaluated V75 geometry, or hide new object and unhide V61 curve.

Reference8 shows the visible lower leg, but overlap of the far leg, shadows and uncalibrated view prevent an exact width measurement. No measured dimensional fidelity is claimed. The 12 mm posterior fullness is an artistic hypothesis, not reconstructed anatomy.

An initial long support changed the insertion-contact pairs with the tunic and was rejected before saving (V83a-calf-rejected-contact.json). Final support is entirely within exposed Z .575–.72, away from ankle/foot and tunic interfaces. Only the visible left calf changes in Y; X, opposite leg, feet, endpoint controls and all other source objects are preserved.

204 vertices changed; maximum11.934mm. Triangle area ratio .996406–1.199465, zero flips or self-intersections. Foot contact67pairs, tunic76pairs, all exactly unchanged (zero new and zero removed). Contact pairs are existing intentional insertion surfaces, not watertight unions.

Paired profile/front renders are600×800,48samples, camera target(.025,-.30,.68), ortho scale.55, same scene lights. Files V75/V83-child-leg-diagnostic-{profile,front}.png.

Self-review: a clear posterior contour change, but the convexity is potentially too prominent and the upper taper looks narrow beneath the hem. This is a technically valid reversible study, NOT an accepted fidelity improvement. Request independent review before retention; do not automatically shrink/grow the same bulge in microversions.
